# Login reads off the game loop (server/README.md "Login reads off the game loop"). The onLogin scripts of the Chaos
# systems and of the base read about 70 result sets per login with db.storeQuery on the game loop (14-15 ms of the 37-39 ms
# login task, p50, with 200 bots on the full map; more when the database is busy). They now run on the login worker.
#   * After a successful game login check (IOLoginData::gameworldAuthenticationAsync, patch 0014, on the worker's own
#     connection of 0029) the worker looks up the character id and runs the SELECTs logins ran before for this player
#     (LoginPrefetch::fetch), copies each result out of the client library (Database::storeRows, struct DBRows) and
#     hands them to the login task. While the onLogin scripts run (Player::onPlacedCreature), Database::storeQuery on
#     the main connection answers a statement with exactly the same text from those rows (DBResult over a DBRows),
#     when no write was committed to a table it reads since the snapshot taken before its read. Everything else (other
#     text, a stale table, a write, a query outside the onLogin scripts, a batch older than 5 s) goes to the database.
#   * Which SELECTs: learnt from the logins (src/chaosprefetch.h Templates): each SELECT of an onLogin script with the
#     player id, the account id and the quoted name taken out (only when the two ids differ). Plain SELECTs of tables of
#     this database only: no comment, user variable, FOR UPDATE / LOCK IN SHARE MODE, INTO, time / random / connection
#     functions, other schemas or stored functions of the database. A template no login ran again is dropped after 2
#     (seen once) or 50 (seen more) prefetches; at most 512 templates, 256 per login.
#   * Write clock (src/chaosprefetch.h WriteClock): a counter per table, raised after each write is committed, on every
#     connection (Database::executeQuery / storeQuery / commit / rollback: the main one, the async query thread's, the
#     login workers'). A write raises its table and the tables its foreign keys (ON DELETE / ON UPDATE CASCADE, SET
#     NULL, SET DEFAULT) and triggers reach, read from information_schema at startup and again after every CREATE /
#     ALTER / DROP / RENAME (src/chaosprefetch.h Dependencies). In a transaction (BEGIN / START TRANSACTION, SET
#     autocommit = 0, DBTransaction) the tables count at its end. A statement that cannot be told apart (multi-table
#     UPDATE / DELETE, CALL, DDL, a comment, ...) raises every table.
#   * config.lua loginPrefetch (default true, read at startup); false: everything as before. The slow task log (0027)
#     shows the answered reads as "db prefetched N". New: src/chaosprefetch.h (pure, tested by
#     server/tools/chaosprefetch_test.cpp in CI), src/loginprefetch.h/.cpp (added to src/CMakeLists.txt).
# Untouched: the scripts, the engine's own player load (IOLoginData::preloadPlayer / loadPlayerById), every write.
# Apply in the server source root after 0001-0030: patch -p1 < 0031-login-reads-prefetch.patch, then rebuild.
